          "code": {
            "language": "markdown",
            "showLineNumbers": false,
            "showMiniMap": false
          },
          "content": "## 📋 Quick Instructions & Notes for Executives & Ops\n\n**How to use this dashboard:**\n- **Filters (top bar)**: Select `Job` / Device Type (e.g. `node` for Linux node-exporter, `windows-exporter` or your Windows job). Use `All` for combined view. Add more variables like `env` or `app` if your Prometheus targets have those labels.\n- **RAG Status**: Colors on CPU% and Memory% columns instantly show health. Red = Critical (action needed), Yellow = Warning (monitor), Green = Healthy.\n- **Drilldown**: Click any **Instance** (hostname) in the table to open a detailed per-server dashboard (update the Data Link URL in the Table panel settings with your actual Grafana detail dashboard UID, e.g. the popular Node Exporter Full ID 1860 or a custom one filtered by host).\n- **Your Excel list**: Cross-reference with the table to ensure all servers from your Excel are appearing (check Prometheus targets or scrape config). Missing ones? Add them to Prometheus `static_configs` or service discovery.\n\n**For Windows servers**: The queries are optimized for standard Linux `node_exporter`. For Windows (`windows_exporter`):\n- Duplicate panels/queries and adapt metrics, e.g.:\n  - CPU: `windows_cpu_time_total` (calculate idle % appropriately, often more involved with core/mode labels)\n  - Memory: `windows_memory_available_bytes` / `windows_memory_total_physical_bytes`\n  - Network: `windows_net_bytes_received_total` etc.\nTest in Explore first. Many teams run both exporters or use Telegraf for unified metrics.\n\n**Customization tips**: \n- Add `app`, `env`, `datacenter` labels via Prometheus relabeling for better \"app level\" grouping.\n- Set up alerts on the Critical stat or table thresholds.\n- For even prettier exec view, consider adding the Status History panel or Boom Table plugin if installed.\n\n**Data freshness**: Auto-refreshes every 30s. Time range default last 1h (adjust top right). Perfect for keeping an eye on things during big events tomorrow! 🚀\n\n*Dashboard created for Prashanth - tailored for executive visibility on app servers & infrastructure health.*",
          "mode": "markdown"
        },
